    "root_cause_analysis": {
      "quantization_failure": "At N=4 demonstrations of length 3 (12 tokens), exact match is quantized in steps of 0.25. Because neural primitives operate at 75-85% token accuracy, a 2-stage composition naturally encounters 1-2 token errors across 12 tokens, reducing sequence exact match to 0.50 (2/4). The discrete Exact-Match threshold of 0.75 and min_margin of 0.05 caused systematic false abstention.",
      "mathematical_origin_of_autonomous_em": "When the engine abstains, it executes an empty plan resulting in 0.0 exact match. The 25% of tasks where it did not abstain achieved 45.83% exact match. Weighted average: 0.25 * 0.4583 + 0.75 * 0.0 = 0.1146 exactly. Controls (WRONG_ORDER at 0.1163, FIXED_ORDER at 0.1076) never abstained, yielding ~11% EM by chance.",
      "small_sample_and_wide_confidence_intervals": "Only 6 unfamiliar instances were tested across 3 seeds (2 per seed). With only 3 seeds (df=2), t_crit=4.303 at 95% confidence, creating confidence intervals exceeding +-0.20 and preventing statistical differentiation from controls."
    },
